    "findings": [
      "The player-bounty Jedi authority is the exact force_title_jedi_rank_02 title skill, not generic force sensitivity or combat level.",
      "Visibility admits normal Jedi bounties at 1500, caps at 8000, decays proportionally over 21 days, and is produced by witnessed Jedi actions with enemy, neutral, and friendly weights of 1.0, 0.5, and 0.25.",
      "Seven production-reachable visibility call sites are authenticated. An eighth textual call in systems/jedi/jedi_base.java is retained legacy compatibility code with no subclass, caller, script attachment, command hook, template reference, or engine event handler in the source tree.",
      "Publish 14.1 bounty value is derived from spent force_discipline skill points and Force rank, with a 25000 unranked floor and 50000 ranked floor; at most five hunters may hold the target.",
      "Mission creation and acceptance revalidate online, bounty, visibility, title/state provenance, hunter count, recent-kill buffer, hunter-target cooldown, self, and account boundaries; no combat-level band is involved. Publish 14.1's enabled-by-default private-structure mission behavior is preserved.",
      "A successful player bounty pays the snapshotted credit reward and grants bountyhunter XP exactly once at reward divided by 50, without the later faction-standing or PvP-rating adjustment.",
      "A successful normal Jedi bounty clears visibility and applies the era Jedi XP loss. NPC bounty fallback remains available when no qualifying player target exists."
    ]
  },
